 "frame_rule": "Each model file has its own frame, fixed by the unit's own shape and not by where the unit goes on the hand: the origin is the centre of the box around the unit; +z is up as the unit lies in its nest; x runs along the long side of the smallest rectangle around the unit's outline seen from above; +x points to the side of that rectangle's centre on which the centroid of the unit's surface lies. The palm base's frame follows the same rule; where it stands on the fixture is in cell_manual.md.",
 "mass_note": "Masses, centres of mass and the links' values are those of the model the cell simulates (design values: printed parts from their volume, bought parts from the parts list); nothing was weighed.",
 "box_note": "box_mm is the size of the unit's solids along x, y and z, centred on the origin; the box of the model file's own triangles agrees with it in size and in centre within 0.02 mm on every axis. collision_box_mm is the box of the convex pieces the cell collides for that unit, with all joints at zero. The pieces themselves are not given (cell_manual.md, Collision model).",
 "joint_note": "Joints as the cell simulates them, all at zero in the model files. pivot_mm is a point of the joint's axis, axis its direction (a positive angle turns the child link about it by the right-hand rule). drive servo: an unpowered servo joint; drive pin: a free pin of the finger's closed four-bar loop. range_loose_rad holds while the module lies loose; range_mounted_rad once it is fastened, for a finger by the place it is mounted in (the palm base stops it differently in each place); range_rad holds in both states. Every range end is a mechanical stop. published_range_rad is the product's data sheet value, for comparison only.",
